serl_controller -- licences and provenance
==========================================

serl_controller is distributed under the MIT License below (the licence of the code it is
ported from). Parts of it, and some files used only by its tests, come from other projects
under their own licences, listed here.

1. SERL's controllers (MIT) -- the package as a whole
-----------------------------------------------------
Ported from rail-berkeley/serl_franka_controllers
(https://github.com/rail-berkeley/serl_franka_controllers), commit 1f140ef:

  src/law.cpp, include/serl_controller/law.hpp
      <- src/cartesian_impedance_controller.cpp, include/serl_franka_controllers/cartesian_impedance_controller.h
  src/params.cpp, include/serl_controller/params.hpp
      <- cfg/compliance_param.cfg
  include/serl_controller/pseudo_inversion.hpp
      <- include/serl_franka_controllers/pseudo_inversion.h (itself a public-domain file by
         Enrico Corvaglia, CentroEPiaggio/kuka-lwr)
  src/joint_reset.cpp, include/serl_controller/joint_reset.hpp (SerlJointPositionLaw)
      <- src/joint_position_controller.cpp, include/serl_franka_controllers/joint_position_controller.h
  src/motion.cpp, src/joint_reset_motion.cpp, include/serl_controller/{motion,joint_reset_motion}.hpp,
  python/bindings.cpp
      run / bind the ports above (new code, same licence).

Verbatim copies, for the golden tests only (not in the wheel): tests/cpp/golden/serl_original/
(its own LICENSE; checksums in SHA256SUMS).

